        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2013",
        "question_text": "<p>Express <math>$\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)}$</math> in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume <math>$\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \frac{A}{x + 1} + \frac{B}{x - 2}$</math>.<br>Multiply through by the denominator: <math>$3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$</math>.<br>Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = -1$ and $x = 2$:<br>$A = 2$, $B = 1$.<br>Thus, the partial fractions are <math>$\frac{2}{x + 1} + \frac{1}{x - 2}$</math>.</p>",
