        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2013",
        "question_text": "<p>Find the derivative of <math>$y = x^3 \\ln x$</math> with respect to $x$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the product rule: <math>$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{d}{dx}(x^3) \\cdot \\ln x + x^3 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln x)$</math>.<br>This gives: <math>$3x^2 \\ln x + x^3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} = 3x^2 \\ln x + x^2$</math>.</p>",
